Scanned libvcodecdrv.so with facts/vcu_usage.py (now includes it): 3 call sites, all __open_2 of /proc/device-tree/chosen/atag,devinfo (0x7626e, 0x778fa, 0x77f9c, O_RDONLY). ZERO ioctl and ZERO mmap calls in the whole 2.2 MB library. All kernel access of the codec stack goes through the OAL in libvcodec_utility.so (eVideo*), so:
- you do not need a separate encoder register-window path: the encoder window is mapped by eVideoMMAP (0x19a40), whose offset comes from the caller's struct;
- the only literal register-window mmap is still vdec_drv_init_hw_info: mmap(NULL, 0x40000, RW, SHARED, fd, 0x16000000);
- /proc/device-tree/chosen/atag,devinfo must return a devinfo string (libvcodecdrv opens it; V33 owns the virtual file).
Updated facts/vcu_usage.md §1/§4 and FACTS.md 5.6a/8.8. Test still N2TEST D01 PASS 32/32.
